 transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(156.5 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(295.088511 27.227294) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" d=\"M 3456 4749 Q 3507 4749 3532 4723 Q 3558 4698 3552 4672 L 3546 4442 Q 3546 4390 3520 4329 Q 3494 4269 3456 4211 Q 3200 3827 2960 3385 Q 2720 2944 2515 2477 Q 2310 2010 2147 1571 Q 1984 1133 1875 758 Q 1766 384 1728 122 Q 1715 0 1632 0 L 1126 0 Q 1024 0 1050 109 Q 1139 467 1289 918 Q 1440 1370 1661 1891 Q 1882 2413 2182 2982 Q 2483 3552 2861 4147 Q 2886 4186 2880 4211 Q 2874 4237 2816 4237 L 339 4237 Q 262 4237 262 4314 L 307 4685 Q 314 4749 403 4749 L 3456 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(68.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" transform=\"translate(89.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(149.609375 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p48c446f1b6\"><rect x=\"43.373\" y=\"11.088\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Extra revenue a year ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>SMS reminders:</b> no-shows fall to 9%: 9,600 more appointments × $90 = $0.86M, less SMS costs $0.02M: <b>+$0.85M</b>.</p> <p><b>Deposits:</b> 5% fewer bookings, but only 5% no-shows: attended appointments = 95% × 95% = 90.25% of today's slots, against 85% now: <b>+$0.76M</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> reminders gain more, cost almost nothing and don't put patients off.</p>"},{"q":"Should Willow also overbook?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>With reminders, about 9% still don't come, so a physio with 16 bookings expects about 1.4 no-shows a day. One extra booking a day would usually be seen in a no-show gap, adding up to about $0.8M a year. But on days when everyone turns up, a patient waits or the physio works late. Use it only for therapists and times with high no-show rates, and use the waiting list to fill late cancellations first.</p>"}],"reco":"No-shows cost Willow about $2.2M a year in lost revenue. Start with SMS reminders the day before: they cut no-shows from 15% to about 9% and add about $0.85M a year for almost no cost, more than deposits ($0.76M), which also put some patients off. Then fill late gaps from the waiting list, and overbook only where no-show rates stay high. Risk: overbooking can make patients wait. Next step: roll out reminders to all clinics this month.","great":["Sizes the problem in dollars","Compares options including their side effects","Counts lost bookings from deposits","Treats overbooking carefully"],"id":80,"slug":"willow-physio"}